            <div class="path-label">Emissions reduction by 2030<br><strong>2°C pathway</strong><br>Net zero CO₂ by ~2070</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pathway-card">
            <div class="path-temp">~500 GtCO₂</div>
            <div class="path-label">Remaining carbon budget<br>for 50% likelihood of<br>limiting warming to 1.5°C</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pathway-card">
            <div class="path-temp" style="font-size:16px; color: var(--text-secondary);">Key Levers</div>
            <div class="path-label" style="text-align:left;">Energy decarbonization &bull; Transport electrification &bull; Demand-side efficiency &bull; Carbon sink protection &amp; restoration</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Narrowing Window -->
      <section class="urgency-section" id="call-to-action" aria-label="The narrowing window for action">
        <h3>The Narrowing Window for Action</h3>
        <div class="urgency-grid">
          <div class="urgency-item"><strong>This decade is decisive.</strong> Choices made now will determine whether warming can be held to 1.5°C or 2°C. Delayed action increases costs, locks in high-carbon infrastructure, and reduces the feasibility of limiting warming.</div>
          <div class="urgency-item"><strong>Climate finance falls short</strong> by a factor of 3 to 6 for adaptation alone. Developing nations remain disproportionately exposed to climate impacts while lacking resources for adaptation.</div>
          <div class="urgency-item"><strong>Immediate, deep, and sustained</strong> emissions reductions across all sectors are essential. Every fraction of a degree matters — each increment of warming intensifies risks and impacts irreversibly.</div>
